{"state": "ALDERMOOR INDUSTRIES SE \u2014 PROCURE-TO-PAY MANUAL, Chapter 9 \"Invoice approval routing\" (rev. 2026-06)\n\n9.1 Purpose. Every supplier invoice must be approved at the correct tier before payment. The tier depends on (a) the vendor's risk category and (b) the invoice amount in EUR, including aggregation (9.5).\n\n9.2 Identifying the vendor. Invoices are matched to a vendor master record through the trading-name alias list (Annex A). Several vendors have similar names; match on the EXACT trading name printed on the invoice, including the legal-form suffix (AG, GmbH, Ltd \u2026). The vendor ID from Annex A is used for every later step.\n\n9.3 Risk category. Start with the category in the vendor master (Annex B). The category is raised to ELEVATED if either of the following is true:\n    (i) the vendor's payee bank account is held in a country that is not in the EU/EEA list in Annex D;\n    (ii) the vendor was onboarded less than 6 months before the invoice date.\n    A vendor already rated ELEVATED stays ELEVATED. No rule lowers a category.\n\n9.4 Currency. Non-EUR invoices are converted at the reference rate for the invoice date in Annex C. Annex C quotes the amount of FOREIGN currency per 1 EUR, so EUR amount = foreign amount \u00f7 rate. Round to cents.\n\n9.5 Aggregation (anti-splitting). The amount used for routing is the current invoice PLUS all earlier invoices from the SAME vendor ID against the SAME purchase order whose invoice dates fall within the 30 calendar days before the current invoice date. Earlier invoices are converted at the rate for their own invoice date.\n\n9.6 Approval matrix (routing amount in EUR):\n| Risk category | Tier 1 Team lead | Tier 2 Department head | Tier 3 CFO           | Tier 4 Board (Finance Committee) |\n|---------------|------------------|------------------------|----------------------|----------------------------------|\n| STANDARD      | \u2264 10,000         | > 10,000 \u2013 50,000      | > 50,000 \u2013 250,000   | > 250,000                        |\n| ELEVATED      | \u2264 5,000          | > 5,000 \u2013 25,000       | > 25,000 \u2013 100,000   | > 100,000                        |\n\n9.7 Other rules. Capex invoices additionally need the asset register number (does not change the tier). Intercompany invoices (vendor IDs starting with IC-) are routed to Group Accounting and are out of scope of this chapter. Invoices without a PO go to the \"no-PO\" exception queue first.\n\nANNEX A \u2014 TRADING-NAME ALIAS LIST (extract)\n| Trading name on invoice            | Vendor ID | Notes |\n|------------------------------------|-----------|-------|\n| Brightwater Facility Ltd           | V-0733    |       |\n| Nordstern Geb\u00e4udeservice GmbH      | V-0981    | also invoices as \"NSG Service GmbH\" |\n| NSG Service GmbH                   | V-0981    |       |\n| NSG Services AG                    | V-1042    | Swiss affiliate of Nordstern; separate legal entity |\n| Nordstern Services AG              | V-1042    |       |\n| Oberland K\u00e4ltetechnik GmbH         | V-1107    |       |\n| Pelham Industrial Supplies Ltd     | V-0655    |       |\n| Rhein-Ruhr Arbeitsschutz GmbH      | V-0870    |       |\n| Aldermoor Services UK Ltd          | IC-0012   | intercompany |\n| Aldermoor Polska Sp. z o.o.        | IC-0019   | intercompany |\n| Castellan Logistics BV             | V-0912    |       |\n| Castellan Logistik GmbH            | V-0913    | German sister company of V-0912 |\n| Dunmore Precision Tools Ltd        | V-0588    |       |\n| Eastbrook IT Services Ltd          | V-1003    | trades as \"EBIT\" on some invoices |\n| EBIT                               | V-1003    |       |\n| Falkenried Sicherheitsdienst GmbH  | V-0764    |       |\n| Gr\u00fcnwald Catering AG               | V-1011    |       |\n| Gr\u00fcnwald Catering GmbH             | V-0689    | not related to V-1011 |\n\nANNEX B \u2014 VENDOR MASTER (extract)\n| Vendor ID | Legal name                        | Seat           | Payee bank country | Onboarded  | Risk (master) |\n|-----------|-----------------------------------|----------------|--------------------|------------|---------------|\n| V-0655    | Pelham Industrial Supplies Ltd    | Leeds, GB      | GB                 | 2019-03-12 | ELEVATED      |\n| V-0733    | Brightwater Facility Ltd          | Dublin, IE     | IE                 | 2021-10-01 | STANDARD      |\n| V-0870    | Rhein-Ruhr Arbeitsschutz GmbH     | Essen, DE      | DE                 | 2016-01-20 | STANDARD      |\n| V-0981    | Nordstern Geb\u00e4udeservice GmbH     | Hamburg, DE    | DE                 | 2018-07-02 | STANDARD      |\n| V-1042    | Nordstern Services AG             | Z\u00fcrich, CH     | CH                 | 2024-05-06 | STANDARD      |\n| V-1107    | Oberland K\u00e4ltetechnik GmbH        | Rosenheim, DE  | AT                 | 2026-05-18 | STANDARD      |\n| V-0588    | Dunmore Precision Tools Ltd       | Sheffield, GB  | GB                 | 2015-09-01 | STANDARD      |\n| V-0689    | Gr\u00fcnwald Catering GmbH            | Munich, DE     | DE                 | 2017-04-11 | STANDARD      |\n| V-0764    | Falkenried Sicherheitsdienst GmbH | Hamburg, DE    | DE                 | 2020-02-03 | ELEVATED      |\n| V-0912    | Castellan Logistics BV            | Rotterdam, NL  | NL                 | 2022-08-15 | STANDARD      |\n| V-0913    | Castellan Logistik GmbH           | Duisburg, DE   | DE                 | 2022-08-15 | STANDARD      |\n| V-1003    | Eastbrook IT Services Ltd         | Bristol, GB    | IE                 | 2023-11-20 | STANDARD      |\n| V-1011    | Gr\u00fcnwald Catering AG              | Basel, CH      | DE                 | 2025-02-01 | STANDARD      |\n\nANNEX C \u2014 REFERENCE RATES (foreign currency per 1 EUR)\n| Date       | CHF    | GBP    | USD    |\n|------------|--------|--------|--------|\n| 2026-07-30 | 0.9551 | 0.8412 | 1.0890 |\n| 2026-08-14 | 0.9437 | 0.8398 | 1.0934 |\n| 2026-08-28 | 0.9412 | 0.8431 | 1.1012 |\n| 2026-09-01 | 0.9405 | 0.8440 | 1.1020 |\n| 2026-09-15 | 0.9390 | 0.8455 | 1.1047 |\n\nANNEX D \u2014 EU/EEA COUNTRY LIST (ISO codes)\nAT, BE, BG, CY, CZ, DE, DK, EE, ES, FI, FR, GR, HR, HU, IE, IS, IT, LI, LT, LU, LV, MT, NL, NO, PL, PT, RO, SE, SI, SK\n\nANNEX E \u2014 INVOICE LEDGER, PO-7710 \"Facility services Z\u00fcrich office\" (all invoices booked against this PO)\n| Invoice no.   | Trading name on invoice       | Invoice date | Amount       | Status   |\n|---------------|-------------------------------|--------------|--------------|----------|\n| NS-2026-071   | NSG Services AG               | 2026-07-30   | CHF 80,000.00| PAID     |\n| NG-2026-5520  | NSG Service GmbH              | 2026-08-14   | EUR 3,950.00 | PAID     |\n| NS-2026-118   | NSG Services AG               | 2026-08-28   | CHF 5,900.00 | PAID     |\n| NS-2026-131   | NSG Services AG               | 2026-09-15   | CHF 21,400.00| TO ROUTE |\n\nANNEX F \u2014 HELPDESK FAQ (excerpt)\nQ: Can I split an invoice into two to stay under a limit? A: No \u2014 see 9.5; splitting is detected by aggregation.\nQ: Does the tier depend on the cost centre? A: No. Cost centre owners are informed but do not change the tier.\nQ: What if a vendor sends a credit note? A: Credit notes are not aggregated and do not reduce the routing amount.\nQ: Are Swiss vendors treated as EU for routing? A: Only the Annex D list counts.\n\nANNEX G \u2014 WORKFLOW SERVICE LEVELS AND DELEGATION\nG.1 Approvers must act within 3 business days (Tier 1\u20132) or 5 business days (Tier 3). Tier 4 items are collected for the next Finance Committee meeting (monthly, second Tuesday).\nG.2 Delegation during absence is allowed only to a person at the SAME or HIGHER tier and must be recorded in the workflow tool before the absence starts. Delegation never changes the tier an invoice is routed to.\nG.3 Early-payment discounts do not justify skipping a tier. If a discount would be lost, the AP clerk may mark the item \"priority\" in the workflow tool.\nG.4 Approval by e-mail is not valid; approvals are only recorded in the workflow tool.\nG.5 If the routing amount lies exactly on a boundary (e.g. EUR 25,000.00 for an ELEVATED vendor), the LOWER tier applies, consistent with the \"\u2264\" and \"> \u2026 \u2013\" notation in 9.6.\nG.6 Re-routing: if a vendor's risk category changes after routing but before approval, the invoice is re-routed using the new category.\n\nANNEX H \u2014 CHANGE LOG\n2026-06-01  9.3(i) extended from \"outside the EU\" to \"outside the EU/EEA\" (Norway, Iceland, Liechtenstein no longer trigger ELEVATED).\n2026-03-15  9.5 window changed from 60 to 30 calendar days.\n2025-11-01  Tier 4 threshold for STANDARD raised from EUR 200,000 to EUR 250,000.\n2025-07-01  Annex C switched from \"EUR per foreign unit\" to \"foreign units per EUR\" quotation; see 9.4.\n\nCASE: route invoice NS-2026-131 (NSG Services AG, CHF 21,400.00, invoice date 2026-09-15, PO-7710, service invoice, not capex).\nAP clerk's draft: \"NSG = Nordstern, standard risk, ~EUR 22.8k \u2192 Tier 2 department head.\"\n", "model": "ruvector-native-submission-round2-v2", "questions": {"decision": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Following Chapter 9, which approval tier must invoice NS-2026-131 be routed to?", "criteria": {"tier1_team_lead": "Route to Tier 1 (team lead).", "tier2_department_head": "Route to Tier 2 (department head).", "tier3_cfo": "Route to Tier 3 (CFO).", "tier4_board": "Route to Tier 4 (Board Finance Committee)."}}}}